      "final_text": "I fixed three defects in `src/durations/__init__.py`, and all 4 tests now pass.\n\n- **Minutes were worth 3600 seconds.** `_UNIT_SECONDS[\"m\"]` is now 60. This caused the wrong results for `1h30m` and the `format_duration` round trip.\n- **Case and whitespace weren't handled.** The regex now allows leading and trailing whitespace and uses `re.IGNORECASE`, so `\" 2M \"` parses.\n- **Trailing garbage was accepted.** `_PATTERN.match` only checked the start of the string, so I switched it to `fullmatch`. Input with stray characters after a valid prefix now raises `ValueError`.",
